\description{
\code{statsnzade} provides a small set of functions for discovering and
downloading data from Stats NZ's \href{https://explore.data.stats.govt.nz/}{Aotearoa Data Explorer}
(ADE) SDMX API, following the same shape as similar packages for other
national statistics agencies (e.g. the \code{cancensus}, \code{OECD} and
\code{rsdmx} packages):
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ade_list]{ade_list()}} lists every available dataset.
\item \code{\link[=ade_search]{ade_search()}} searches dataset ids and descriptions.
\item \code{\link[=ade_dims]{ade_dims()}} returns a dataset's dimensions and their allowed
codes.
\item \code{\link[=ade_data]{ade_data()}} downloads data, optionally filtered by dimension
codes and/or a time range.
\item \code{\link[=ade_meta]{ade_meta()}} gets a dataset's name, description, and dimension
ids, and renders them as a browsable overview.
}

Dataset and dimension metadata changes rarely but is expensive to
fetch, so it is cached locally the first time it's needed; see
\code{\link[=ade_cache_info]{ade_cache_info()}}.
}
\section{Authentication}{

Requests to the ADE API require a subscription key. Set it once per
session with \code{\link[=ade_api]{ade_api()}}, or set the \code{SNZ_PRIMARY_KEY} environment
variable (e.g. in \code{.Renviron}) so it's picked up automatically.

Subscribe to Stats NZ Aotearoa Data Explorer at
\url{https://portal.apis.stats.govt.nz/}
}

